
Valid Submissions
Health check up packages are eligible for reimbursement.
Diagnostic tests included as part of the health check up are eligible.
Home sample collection charges can be claimed.
Doctor consultation is valid only if it is part of the check up package.
Invoice must be in the associates name.
Invoice date must fall within Apr 1, 2026 to Mar 31, 2027.
Claim amount must be within the age-based limit (INR 3,750 for <35; INR 4,750 for 35+).
Multiple claims are allowed as long as the total does not exceed the annual limit.
Invalid Submissions
Health check ups for dependents cannot be claimed.
Standalone doctor consultations are not eligible.
Prescribed or OTC medication cannot be reimbursed.
Medical equipment, devices, or therapy are not covered.
Hospitalization or emergency medical expenses are not eligible.
Any medical cost outside the defined coverage is invalid.
Invoices not in the associates name are not accepted.
Invoices without a valid date or outside the policy period will be rejected.
Handwritten receipts are not accepted.
Non GST vendor invoices that do not qualify as tax invoices are invalid.
Incorrectly uploaded or non PDF documents are not accepted.
Claims that exceed the annual reimbursement limit are invalid.
Claims submitted after the policy deadline will be rejected.
Fake receipts or altered documents are strictly prohibited.
Claims for dependents, family, or others are invalid.
Transferring purchased services to another person is not permitted.
Payment gateway or convenience fees cannot be claimed.
Any cost not directly part of the health check up is invalid.
Claims from outside India are not allowed (if restrictions apply).
Unused balance cannot be carried forward to the next year
